          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nóngcūn is built from nóng 'farming' and cūn 'village', both inherited from Middle Chinese, nowng and tshwon (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'farming the fields' and the second 'a farmstead'."
            }
